out.push(A('⚠ **Two counts and the band.** **Connectives before and after:** **one to eleven, with removals of one to five, and an average gain of nine words** — **which the room should hear, because nobody does this for the word count.** **Then: where did your reader say the piece changes its mind?** **Six of ten named the intended place, two named a place with no turn in it, and two found none** — **and those four are the useful half of the lesson.**'));

// ===================== 23.3 =====================
out.push(pb());
out.push(h2('23.3  One thread, eight paragraphs, and not its name'));
out.push(S('Stage 1 · Get ready'));
out.push(A('**a** Open, with the search box. ⚠ **The counts ran from six to thirty-one and nobody had counted before being asked.** **Then the question that does the cycle\'s work: whose piece is about that phrase?** **In every case it is** — **and the room should see that the most repeated phrase and the thread are the same thing, which is why the repetition felt necessary while it was being written.**'));
out.push(A('**b** Carry the thread forward: **2** and **4**. ⚠ **One adds a year, the other adds a reader.** **1, 3 and 5 mark time** — **_the aforementioned_, the ninth repetition, and _this issue_, which is the worst of the three because it names nothing at all and could refer to any noun in the paragraph.**'));
out.push(NOTE('⚠ **The rule is that every mention which is not the name must advance, and the fault it produces is new, so watch for it: a description that marks time is worse than the name it replaced, because it looks like progress.** **Three of Mrs Tarabishi\'s fourteen said the same thing, and her partner found all four duplicates in nine minutes by reading only the descriptions, in order, with nothing between them.** ⚠ **Run exactly that in Stage 3: the writer reads their advancing descriptions aloud, in order, and nothing else.** **A writer cannot do this to their own piece** — **and naming the procedure is worth more to the room than finding the four, which is why the model describes the method and not only the result.**'));
out.push(NOTE('⚠ **Protect the term, because one student in ten has a word that cannot be replaced and will be told to replace it.** **_Write-off_, _establishment_, _district rule_: a term is the same word every time and precision is the point.** **A thread is what the piece is carrying.** ⚠ **Where the two are the same word, the name stays and the advancing is done by the facts attached to it** — **and nine of Mrs Tarabishi\'s thirty-one mentions stayed for exactly that reason: a definition, four figures, three disagreements and one sentence about what a reader may not take.** **A writer who cannot list the places where the name stays is not keeping it for a reason.**'));
out.push(S('Language box · Practise'));
out.push(A('**1** _The aforementioned figure_ → ⚠ **marks time, is longer than the name, and points backwards.**   **2** _The figure nobody has recomputed since 2011_ → **advances; adds a year.**   **3** ⚠ **The ninth repetition** → **the drum.**   **4** _This issue_ → **names nothing.**   **5** ⚠ **A term that cannot be replaced** → **keep it, and advance with the facts beside it.**'));
out.push(S('Stage 3 · Practise (sample – Card A)'));
